      "source_text": "Last week in true Relativity Space fashion we said Good Luck, Have Fun to our Additive Development interns as they head back to school. This was my first time as a formal intern manager, and I was incredibly impressed with how big of an impact our interns made in such a short time. I learned a lot about the balance of leadership and technical work, making sure that we are achieving our milestones while building a team that works well together and plays to the strengths of each individual. Cinco Murchison I really enjoyed working with you this summer, thank you for your eagerness to learn and the lasting contributions you have made to our manufacturing processes. It always feels like our interns leave us before we are ready, and we hope this is not goodbye but see you later. Whether that’s here at Relativity next year or our paths crossing further down the road, we are proud of you and are cheering you on from the sidelines in all of your academic and professional endeavors!",
